.SH "\fR3\&.1\&.0\fP"
.PP
\fR\fP

.PP
\fR
.IP "\(bu" 2
Fixed numerous bugs in attribute nodes relating to the handling of comments and whitespace\&. There's significant changes to \fRattrNode\&.spaces\fP and \fRattrNode\&.raws\fP since the \fR3\&.0\&.0\fP release\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Added \fRAttribute#offsetOf(part)\fP to get the offset location of attribute parts like \fR"operator"\fP and \fR"value"\fP\&. This is most often added to \fRAttribute#sourceIndex\fP for error reporting\&.
.PP
\fP

.PP
\fR\fP
.SH "\fR3\&.0\&.0\fP"
.PP
\fR\fP

.PP
\fR\fP
.SS "\fRBreaking changes\fP"
\fR\fP

.PP
\fR
.IP "\(bu" 2
Some tweaks to the tokenizer/attribute selector parsing mean that whitespace locations might be slightly different to the 2\&.x code\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Better attribute selector parsing with more validation; postcss-selector-parser no longer uses regular expressions to parse attribute selectors\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Added an async API (thanks to @jacobp100); the default \fRprocess\fP API is now async, and the sync API is now accessed through \fRprocessSync\fP instead\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRprocess()\fP and \fRprocessSync()\fP now return a string instead of the Processor instance\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Tweaks handling of Less interpolation (thanks to @jwilsson)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Removes support for Node 0\&.12\&.
.PP
\fP

.PP
\fR\fP
.SS "\fROther changes\fP"
\fR\fP

.PP
\fR
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRast()\fP and \fRastSync()\fP methods have been added to the \fRProcessor\fP\&. These return the \fRRoot\fP node of the selectors after processing them\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRtransform()\fP and \fRtransformSync()\fP methods have been added to the \fRProcessor\fP\&. These return the value returned by the processor callback after processing the selectors\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Set the parent when inserting a node (thanks to @chriseppstein)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Correctly adjust indices when using insertBefore/insertAfter (thanks to @tivac)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Fixes handling of namespaces with qualified tag selectors\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRprocess\fP, \fRast\fP and \fRtransform\fP (and their sync variants) now accept a \fRpostcss\fP rule node\&. When provided, better errors are generated and selector processing is automatically set back to the rule selector (unless the \fRupdateSelector\fP option is set to \fRfalse\fP\&.)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Now more memory efficient when tokenizing selectors\&.
.PP
\fP

.PP
\fR\fP
.SS "\fRUpgrade hints\fP"
\fR\fP

.PP
\fRThe pattern of:\fP

.PP
\fR\fRrule\&.selector = processor\&.process(rule\&.selector)\&.result\&.toString();\fP\fP

.PP
\fRis now:\fP

.PP
\fR\fRprocessor\&.processSync(rule)\fP\fP

.PP
